          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वियोगः — viyogaḥ — \"a separation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जलौघे कुटुम्बस्य वियोगः अभवत्। jalaughe kuṭumbasya viyogaḥ abhavat. In the flood the family was separated."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वियोगः (viyogaḥ) is built from vi, \"apart\", and the root √yuj, \"to join\"; MW gives viyoga as disjunction, separation, and the loss of something (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
